european union ministers responsible for  energy policy have agreed on new rules  to make the use of biofuels in the eu  more sustainable  and so help cut greenhouse gas emissions  it means the council's established its  position on so-called  indirect land use change this is when  farmland is used to produce biofuels  leading to food or feed being grown in  other areas like forests  which results in more carbon dioxide in  the atmosphere  the aims to minimize the environmental  impact of indirect land use  and encourage more advanced biofuels  onto the market  thanks to this common position this  means that in our forthcoming  negotiations with the european  parliament  we can start negotiations on the second  reading of the italian presidency  energy prices were also up for  discussion the ministers examined ways  to strengthen the role  rights and awareness of consumers  preventing the unfair disconnection of  people's electricity was also an area of  concern  energy security in europe in particular  avoiding any major disruption in  supplies next winter and the conflict in  ukraine  was debated too russia is the eu's  biggest natural gas supplier  much of which transits through ukraine  the two countries are locked in a gas  price dispute that simmered for several  years and hit supplies  into europe in the past
 

